# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF.
#
# Without this, Git honours a Windows contributor's `core.autocrlf=true` and
# checks the tree out with CRLF, while the committed blobs stay LF. Nothing is
# wrong with the repository when that happens, but `pnpm format:check` then
# fails on ~180 files a Windows checkout never touched, and every `git diff`
# prints "LF will be replaced by CRLF". CI runs on Linux and would not see
# either. Pinning the checkout here keeps the two platforms in agreement.
#
# The committed blobs are already LF, so this needs no renormalisation — a
# fresh clone or checkout picks it up.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be converted.
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.keystore binary
*.jar binary
*.zip binary
*.hbc binary

# The Gradle wrapper's Windows launcher is the one file that needs CRLF.
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
